Subject: simple: reset shared qcom-camss links before selecting a camera

The SM8550 CAMSS exposes all four sensors through shared CSID and VFE sink
pads. Camera discovery leaves the last sensor path enabled, and the routing
heuristic skips some conflicting links on routing-capable entities. The next
camera then fails to configure with EBUSY while enabling its CSIPHY link.

The simple pipeline already serializes cameras that share pads. Reset all
mutable CAMSS links before enabling the selected path so switching cameras
also works across independent PipeWire clients.

X716B camera bring-up session: at the exact pinned commit
(62d4bfc450798cbd57722fa349a245b93b11d1cd), CameraSensor::entity() is
`virtual const MediaEntity *entity() const`, so ->device() resolves to
MediaDevice's const overload and calling the non-const disableLinks() on it
is a hard C++ error (discards qualifiers), not just a warning -Werror could
be blamed for -- confirmed by a real build failure on this project's own
Fedora rootfs build. A const_cast is needed to route around the const
accessor to the same live, mutable MediaDevice the pipeline handler already
holds non-const references to elsewhere (see locateSensors()).

--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -764,6 +764,17 @@ int SimpleCameraData::setupLinks()
 {
 	int ret;

+	/* Qualcomm CAMSS sensors share receiver sink pads. Camera enumeration
+	 * leaves the final sensor path enabled, which can make the first real
+	 * configure fail with EBUSY. Cameras sharing those pads are serialized
+	 * by this pipeline handler, so clear the graph before selecting one. */
+	if (sensor_->entity()->device()->driver() == "qcom-camss") {
+		ret = const_cast<MediaDevice *>(sensor_->entity()->device())
+			      ->disableLinks();
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Configure all links along the pipeline. Some entities may not allow
 	 * multiple sink links to be enabled together, even on different sink
